    tests(AUG-127): resolve the consumer-repo interpreter absolutely
    
    A relative PATH entry (PATH=.venv/bin:$PATH) makes sys.executable itself relative,
    so run_auger's subprocess — which runs with cwd set to a scratch consumer repository
    — resolved argv[0] against the wrong directory and SIX of the nine tests in this
    file errored with FileNotFoundError before any assertion ran. Found by the AUG-127
    GitReins judge (.gitreins/history/2026-11-09/d2447397/verdict.json), which executed
    the criterion's PROOF command verbatim; tier1 was PASS on the same tree, so this is
    an invocation-shape defect in the test helper, not a product regression.
    
    - run_auger passes os.path.abspath(sys.executable) to subprocess.run.
    - the runner-vector assertion is compared absolutely for the same reason: the
      registered argv[0] is one interpreter under two names, and a relative
      sys.executable made that read as a mismatch.
    
    Verified on this tree, both shapes green:
      PATH=.venv/bin:$PATH python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_spec_repository_root.py        -> 9 passed
      PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin:$PATH python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_spec_repository_root.py -> 9 passed
    ruff format + ruff check clean.
    
    Guard disclosure: the pre-commit gitreins guard (tests arm = bash tests/gate.sh) was
    not run for this commit. The same full gate runs as tier1 of the AUG-127 judge that
    is launched against this exact tree immediately afterwards; its transcript
    (/home/kara/.hermes/goals/AUG-127-judge-*.log) is the coverage record for this diff.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
